\noindent \emph{Inner \eqref{item:flat-frame-relations-2} and outer \eqref{item: FR outer} frame relations}.
\ignore{Let $P$ be an inner frame pattern in $Q'$. If it is not contained in $Q$, then its top corners are 0's and the corresponding frame relation holds. Moreover, such a pattern is not part of an outer frame pattern. 
