\noindent\textbf{Cross-Attn Map.}
As shown in Figure~\ref{fig:attn_map},  our model assigns high attention scores to semantically expressive regions, such as “work,” “waiting,” and the elongated syllables in “so-o-o-o,” demonstrating its ability to capture both word-level semantics and prosodic emphasis. Unlike previous approaches with diffuse or noisy attention, our speech-queried mechanism produces focused and interpretable patterns. The attention selectively highlights gesture-relevant frames while de-emphasizing idle motions, enabling more effective masking and improving alignment between speech and motion.



