\begin{theorem}
\label{D-N} 
Let $\Omega$ be a complete, separable, metric space (Polish space), and let $(\K, D(\K))$ be a linear operator on $C_b(\Omega)$. The following are equivalent:
\begin{itemize}
% [before=\setlength{\baselineskip}{27pt},itemsep=-10pt]
\item $(\K, D(\K))$ is the Koopman generator of a jointly continuous, global flow in $\Omega$. 
\item $(\K, D(\K))$ is a derivation (i.e., $\K(fg) = (\K f)g+f(\K g)$ for all $f,g\in D(\K)$ and generates a bi-continuous semigroup with respect to $\tau$ induced by a jointly continuous flow.
\end{itemize}
In particular, Koopman semigroups induced by jointly continuous, global flows in a Polish space $\Omega$ are bi-continuous contractions in $(C_b(\Omega),\|\cdot\|_\infty,\tau). $  
\end{theorem}
