Branch-and-bound \citep{morrison2016branch} solvers
%is a powerful search technique for finding optimal solutions to mathematical programs, and is a key component of modern nonlinear optimization software. One advantage of this class of algorithms is the ability 
are commonly used to maintain upper and lower bounds on the minimal objective value of any linear or nonlinear MIP,
