\subsection{BEM dataset}
\label{subsec:bem_dataset}
We follow the BEM implementation proposed by Ning \cite{ning_2014} to construct a $(P,\omega, V_a)$ dataset.
The simulation input is the propeller parameters, the freestream velocity, which is varied from \qty{0}{} to \qty[per-mode=symbol]{30}{\meter\per\second}, and the propeller rotational speed, which is varied from \qty{1000}{} to \qty{10000}{\rpm}. The simulation output is the propeller power.
The propeller parameters are measured from the propeller of the test vehicle, presented in \cref{subsec:flight_dataset}, thereby enabling direct comparison of the results.
