\label{sec:statistics}

In the study detailed in Table \ref{Tab:statistics}, we examine the efficacy of adapting a model to a test set by employing training statistics derived from another dataset. Our findings demonstrate that adaptation using training statistics from clean datasets consistently enhances model performance. This improvement is observed even when the training statistics are sourced from a dataset different from that of the test set. We observe that utilizing training statistics from either dataset for adaptation to the test set of the other incurs only a minimal performance decrement. This suggests robustness in model performance to variations in training statistics.

