\subsubsection{Spatial Origins}

As depicted in \cref{fig_rs}, the respiratory tract is divided into the \ac{URT} and the \ac{LRT}.
The \ac{URT} comprises the mouth (oral cavity), nose (nasal cavity), pharynx, and larynx, while the \ac{LRT} includes the trachea, right and left primary bronchi, and lungs~\cite{ahookhoshDevelopmentHumanRespiratory2020}. 

