% Ventilation systems, such as air conditioning units, introduce localized currents or turbulence.
% Human activity, including movements or turning, can then compound these effects and cause abrupt changes in the distribution of airborne particles~\cite{wongEffectsMedicalStaffs2022}. \db{The above content looks very similar to the Ambient Breath Analysis.}

Finally, the detection systems introduce inherent noise due to sensor variability affected by flow rate, binding efficiency, and air velocity~\cite{bhardwaj2021recent}. 
Sudden events such as coughing or sneezing add further disruptions through burst particle emission into the channel~\cite{khalidModelingViralAerosol2020}.

\subsection{Breath Cloud}

