At first, analyzing when a new PP happens and how long a PW takes is not as straightforward as in a single-threaded executor. Moreover, it would be hard to determine how many PWs each callback would take to complete its execution and how many PWs exist between two consecutive callbacks. The difficulty multiplies when chains with arbitrary deadlines are considered. 
