Instead, in this paper, we take a different approach: analyzing the response time of a chain without having PW in mind. Our proposed analysis is built by extending the conventional non-preemptive global task scheduling analysis~\cite{lee14improvement} and taking into account semantic differences introduced by chains, callback dependencies, and the ReadySet management. This approach also allows us to incorporate priority-driven scheduling enhancements that yield a significant benefit to critical chains.   

