\begin{lemma}\label{lm:block}
Consider two adjacent callbacks of a chain $\Gamma_\mathcal{C}$, $\tau_{\langle \mathcal{C},j \rangle}$ and $\tau_{\langle \mathcal{C},j +1 \rangle}$, on a $m$-threaded executor. The precedence-dependency blocking caused by $\tau_{\langle \mathcal{C},j \rangle}$ introduces an additional workload as interference to the start of $\tau_{\langle \mathcal{C},j+1 \rangle}$, which is upper-bounded by
\begin{equation} \label{eq:block}
    B_{\langle \mathcal{C}, j+1 \rangle} = m \cdot E_{\langle \mathcal{C}, j \rangle}
\end{equation}
