		& $\leq \frac{13}{30}n +\Oh(1)$ (\Cref{prop:match+comp})  & $\leq\frac{4}{15}n + \Oh(1)$ (\Cref{prop:combined upper bounds})
	\end{tabular}
	\caption{Summary of bounds on triangles separating bichromatic planar point sets of $n$ points in total.}
	\label{table:results}
\end{table}


We show that \nameref{prb:blue_overlap} and \sloppy \nameref{prb:blue_no_overlap} are NP-hard. Then we prove combinatorial bounds on the number of triangles required for the problems in the worst case for $n$ points, see \Cref{table:results}. The paper is organized in the following manner. Section~\ref{sec:np-hard} describes the hardness of the problems by a polynomial time reduction from the \textsc{Planar Monotone 3-SAT} problem. Section~\ref {sec:bounds} presents an overview of the combinatorial results. 
%This section contains a computational approach to establish the lower bound of the minimum number of triangles in~\cref{prb:both_no_overlap}. Section~\ref{sec:computational} has the details of the computational aspects. 
Finally, the paper is concluded in Section~\ref{sec:concl}. For detailed proofs we refer to the Appendix.
